    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who headline our daily efficiency scores at 76.04 and 74.56, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** faces an elite arm in Cole, but his 16% park factor benefit and optimal #3 slot in the order provide enough insulation to overcome the pitcher's skill. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Bradish; his 16% park edge and a dynamic platoon advantage make him our premier leverage play for both power and potential stolen base production. **Heliot Ramos** (67.47) also warrants attention, as his placement in the #3 hole against Bradish provides a robust opportunity to capitalize on the same favorable park conditions fueling the rest of our infield.\n\nStrategic pacing dictates our final bench decisions, particularly with **Nasim Nunez** (39.47) narrowly missing the cut. While **Nasim Nunez** provides high-end sprint speed\u2014a core priority for this team\u2014his matchup against the high-velocity threat of deGrom dragged his projection below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" We are effectively punting his potential stolen base upside to avoid the efficiency trap posed by a pitcher who suppresses xwOBA significantly. Elsewhere, **Drake Baldwin** (65.45) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) secure their spots in the lineup; **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s #1 spot combined with a high SP skill rating against Holmes provides a solid bridge to the middle of our order, while **Drake Baldwin** earns his start through a strong 0.380 xwOBA and consistent recency performance.\n\nRisk management remains critical for the remainder of the roster, as **Luis Lara** (41.15) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.99) face varying degrees of volatility. **Luis Lara** is teetering on our start-sit threshold due to an unfavorable #9 batting position against Kirby, making him a candidate for an early hook if his first two at-bats fail to produce. We remain cautious of the weather patterns impacting the ballparks hosting **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos**, but provided no late-breaking alerts, these rotations offer the best statistical path to winning our 5x5 categories. With **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined by team off-days, our reliance on the speed-efficient trio of **Sam Antonacci**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Gunnar Henderson** will be the deciding factor in maintaining our category lead.",
